[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. System capabilities

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-003-MILUAV
TITLE: Flight Control Capabilities
STATEMENT: The system provides autonomous takeoff, landing, waypoint navigation, formation flying, and emergency procedures for military operations.
RATIONALE: Flight control capabilities enable autonomous UAV operations.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-004-MILUAV
TITLE: Mission Management Capabilities
STATEMENT: The system provides mission planning, real-time adaptation, payload management, and mission abort procedures with safety interlocks.
RATIONALE: Mission management capabilities enable complex military operations.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-005-MILUAV
TITLE: Communication Capabilities
STATEMENT: The system provides secure communication, encrypted video streaming, and anti-jamming capabilities for military environments.
RATIONALE: Communication capabilities ensure reliable command and control.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Security Capabilities
STATEMENT: The system provides multi-factor authentication, role-based access control, and threat detection for military security requirements.
RATIONALE: Security capabilities protect system integrity and mission data.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. User instructions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-007-MILUAV
TITLE: System Startup
STATEMENT: Users shall follow the startup sequence: power on, system initialization, authentication, mission planning, and pre-flight checks.
RATIONALE: Proper startup ensures safe system operation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-008-MILUAV
TITLE: Mission Planning
STATEMENT: Users shall plan missions using the ground control station interface with waypoint definition, payload configuration, and contingency planning.
RATIONALE: Mission planning ensures successful mission execution.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-009-MILUAV
TITLE: Flight Operations
STATEMENT: Users shall monitor flight operations through the ground control station with real-time telemetry, video feeds, and mission status updates.
RATIONALE: Flight operations monitoring ensures mission success and safety.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-010-MILUAV
TITLE: Emergency Procedures
STATEMENT: Users shall follow emergency procedures for communication loss, system failures, and mission abort with automatic return-to-base capabilities.
RATIONALE: Emergency procedures ensure system and mission safety.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Operational procedures

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-011-MILUAV
TITLE: Pre-Flight Procedures
STATEMENT: Pre-flight procedures include system checks, sensor calibration, communication verification, and mission parameter validation.
RATIONALE: Pre-flight procedures ensure system readiness.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-012-MILUAV
TITLE: In-Flight Procedures
STATEMENT: In-flight procedures include mission monitoring, real-time adaptation, payload deployment, and communication management.
RATIONALE: In-flight procedures ensure mission success.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-013-MILUAV
TITLE: Post-Flight Procedures
STATEMENT: Post-flight procedures include data download, system shutdown, maintenance checks, and mission debriefing.
RATIONALE: Post-flight procedures ensure system maintenance and mission analysis.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM-014-MILUAV
TITLE: Training Requirements
STATEMENT: Users shall complete military UAV operator training and system-specific training before operating the Military Quad Copter RTOS.
RATIONALE: Training requirements ensure safe and effective system operation.

[[/SECTION]] 